Creating User Accounts, Groups, and Root Credentials

1. Create /etc/passwd with root and standard pseudo-user accounts:

cat << 'EOF' > /etc/passwd
root:x:0:0:root:/root:/bin/sh
daemon:x:1:1:daemon:/usr/sbin:/bin/false
bin:x:2:2:bin:/bin:/bin/false
nobody:x:65534:65534:nobody:/:/bin/false
EOF

2. Create /etc/group with core system security groups:

cat << 'EOF' > /etc/group
root:x:0:
daemon:x:1:
bin:x:2:
sys:x:3:
adm:x:4:
tty:x:5:
disk:x:6:
wheel:x:10:
nogroup:x:65534:
EOF

3. Initialize shadow authentication with secure permissions:

touch /etc/shadow
chmod 600 /etc/shadow

cat << 'EOF' > /etc/shadow
root::19000:0:99999:7:::
daemon:*:19000:0:99999:7:::
bin:*:19000:0:99999:7:::
nobody:*:19000:0:99999:7:::
EOF

4. Set password for the root user:

passwd root
